**Convention 81.1 (literal traffic and simultaneous backing).** All preceding accounts concern one actual source and observer realization. Use §§17,65's actual codec, with $\operatorname{bitlen}(0)=1$. For a reduced rational $n/d$, $d>0$, the payload length is

$$
\operatorname{len}_{\mathbb Q}(n/d)
=2\operatorname{bitlen}(|n|)+2\operatorname{bitlen}(d)+3.
\tag{81.1}
$$

A valid nonnegative raw selector $j$ costs $2\operatorname{bitlen}(j)+1$ bits. A growth request at $p$ costs $2|p|+4$, its success reply $2|p|+5$, and each distinct refusal five. Add every actual tag, selector, signed rational, ACK, End, local acknowledgement, Return, address/navigation packet, inner/outward relay and distinct copy at its actual multiplicity. Noncanonical input pays its actual bytes. Zero operands and zero replies are nonempty packets; computing a predicted germ is not a literal source Read. Input reception, original/current reports, reconstructed words, causal data, metrics, germs and Time exports all have construction and transfer costs beyond the displayed source calls.

Let $W_{\rm run}$ be the actual maximum bit width of all source/observer/provider values, numerators, denominators, pivots, determinant denominators, controls, selectors, counters and outputs in the chosen finite run. The arithmetic bounds below count exact rational operations; bit costs include actual-width arithmetic and normalization at this width. Arbitrary rational entries have no dimension-only width bound. A finite binary word gives growing integer widths, not fixed precision: two late scalars and the receiver's other dependent data must distinguish $2^m$ length-$m$ words, so they need at least $m$ bits of distinguishing capacity, and some length-$m$ input requires a binary record of length at least $m$. Two scalar Reads are not two bits.

For every actual Tick on a tree with $N$ cells, a literal implementation zeros $N$ new slots and performs $2(N-1)$ directed neighbour additions, with actual buffer writes. Its observer's separate predicted update is additional work. For §76's credited binary decoder, §65.2 supplies sparse moment generation, finite greedy comparison/subtraction and $O(N(m+I+1))$ further arithmetic work for polynomial evaluation and advancement to the actual endpoint. Its moment weights, both literal scalars, decoded digits/output and vector scratch have their actual widths and coexistence costs under §65.3. Simultaneous backing includes the source old/new field, predictor old/new field, retained graph/raw/canonical maps, code/control, parser and pending frames, references/grants, provider input/control, isolated archives, caller-retained outputs and every live scratch array. Count a physically shared allocation once only when it is actually shared; count distinct coexisting copies separately. Clearing pays writes and leaves retained allocated capacity in the bill. Finite programmes and finite individual completions imply no fixed bound on lifetime memory, precision, references or future backing.

